cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you cite or build on this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Trading Library — a scientific paper series on options, volatility, market mechanics, and quantitative method"
authors:
  - family-names: "Löffler"
    given-names: "Jonas"
    email: "loefflerjonas6@gmail.com"
type: dataset
version: "1.0"
date-released: "2026-09-20"
license: CC-BY-4.0
abstract: >
  A public series of self-written scientific papers (levels L1–L3, English and
  German) covering options mechanics and the greeks, dealer hedging flows and
  GEX, volatility and the VIX complex, statistics and backtesting methodology,
  overfitting control and forecast calibration, macro regimes, systematic and
  dealer flows, and algorithm build/run/kill discipline. Every empirical number
  is reproducible from free, publicly retrievable data with the accompanying
  figure scripts. Corrections are tracked in ERRATA.md and CHANGELOG.md.
keywords:
  - options
  - greeks
  - gamma exposure
  - volatility
  - variance risk premium
  - backtesting
  - overfitting
  - calibration
  - quantitative finance
